BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:“Idomeneo” by Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261115T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261115T235900
UID:2d169043d25af9b8d94431663a1ad049@ipm.org
DESCRIPTION:LOVE VS. DUTY\n After King Idomeneo returns to Crete from the 
 Trojan War\, the high-stakes consequences of a desperate deal he struck wi
 th Neptune for safe passage reveal themselves when he must choose between 
 his own son\, Idamante\, and the vow he made to the sea god\, further comp
 licated as Idamante is loved by both the Trojan princess Ilia and the jeal
 ous Greek princess Elettra. But when divine wrath is incurred\, Idamante a
 nd Ilia prove their worth\, prompting Neptune’s mercy.\n Based on a 1705
  play by Crébillion père\, Mozart’s first mature opera demonstrates hi
 s mastery of orchestration\, accompanied recitatives\, and lyrical beauty.
  While it premiered in 1781 in Munich\, it did not see its U.S. premiere u
 ntil 1947\, at Tanglewood.\n Artistic Staff\nConductor\nArthur Fagen\n Sta
 ge Director\nRobin Guarino\n Set Designer\nAndrew Boyce\n Costume Designer
 \nJessica Pabst\n Lighting Designer\nThomas Hase\n Video Designer\nNichola
 s Hussong\n Wig & Makeup Designer\nAndrew Elliot\n Chorus Master\nLisa Has
 son\n Diction Coach\nStefano de Peppo\n Supertitle Author\nCori Ellison\nT
 ickets: https://am.ticketmaster.com/iumac/buy
LOCATION:Musical Arts Center\, 201 S. Eagleson Ave\, Bloomington\, Indiana
  47405
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/idomeneo-by-wolfgang-amad
 eus-mozart-11-09-2026-14-19-10
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
