 9d110cc38872e6%2F2026-dpu-symphonic-band-bw7x5m.png
DESCRIPTION:Presented by DePauw University Institute of Music\n"A Harvest 
 of Sounds and Colors"\nCraig Paré\, conductor\nSunday\, Nov. 15 • 4 p.m
 .\nGreen Center\, Kresge Auditorium\n The DePauw Symphonic Band\, conducte
 d by director of bands Craig Paré\, presents its fall concert featuring p
 ieces voted on by the band members themselves. Among their selections are 
 the New Orleans jazz-inspired "Country Club Stomp\," English folk song "Gr
 eensleeves\," a rousing "March of Freedom\," and "The Magic of Harry Potte
 r\," an iconic medley of themes from all eight Harry Potter films. \n The 
 musicians encourage audience members to bring a non-perishable food item t
 o the concert\, 100% of which will be donated to the Putnam County Emergen
 cy Food Pantry.\nTickets: https://dpugreencenter.eventbrite.com/
LOCATION:DePauw University Green Center\, 600 South Locust St\, GREENCASTL
 E\, Indiana 46135
