BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SIWE (Southern Indiana Wind Ensemble) Fall Concert 11/16/2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261116T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261116T200000
UID:0f625202155588be9d63e94ac9f407d7@ipm.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/db9c
 951/2147483647/strip/true/crop/1545x2000+0+0/resize/254x329!/quality/90/?u
 rl=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3a%2F3e%2Fac1d147a47d9a4
 a8fcec5bb7e242%2Fsiwe-11-16-26.png
DESCRIPTION:Presented by SIWE (Southern Indiana Wind Ensemble)\nThe concer
 t is titled Viva Music! Part of what we do is to emphasize the joy of maki
 ng and listening to live music\, played by real people (us). We all have s
 o much access to music at our fingertips on-line and can have “easy” l
 istening experiences. However\, nothing replaces experiencing music making
  in person\, and we hope that continues for a long time. \nFor our premier
 e this concert we’ll play the final two movements from Erida Svanoe’s 
 Alice in Wonderland. Gordon Jacob’s classic wind band piece\, An Origina
 l Suite\, has a local tie as we’re playing the performance edition by Ch
 ris Heidenreich\, one of our DM Wind Conducting graduates from the Jacobs 
 School of Music. We’re also doing a major repertoire piece\, Toccata Mar
 ziale\, a brilliant work by Ralph Vaughan Williams. Steven Bryant’s beau
 tiful Dusk is a wonderful piece of beauty and reflection. Home of the Brav
 e was composed for the “America 250” celebrations. In that Americana s
 pirit we open with Russell Alexander’s march\,Colossus of Columbia. Viva
  Musica by Alfred Reed epitomizes the concert’s theme with infectious me
 lodies and rhythms\, and our look into Broadway music continues with a gre
 at Warren Barker arrangement: Bricusse and Newley on Broadway.
LOCATION:Bloomington High School North Auditorium\, 3901 N Kinser Pike\, B
 loomington\, Indiana 47404
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/siwe-southern-indiana-win
 d-ensemble-fall-concert-11-16-2026-13-10-2026-17-09-08
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
