BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:T. Scot Halpin Archive 2026 Open House and Holiday Art Sale
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261121T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261121T170000
UID:6568c927b9c8947e0b0ceb9a4a234695@ipm.org
DESCRIPTION:Presented by T. Scot Halpin Archive\nEvery year\, the T. Scot 
 Halpin Archive opens its doors to the community for its Annual Open House 
 and Holiday Art Sale\, being held this year on November 21\, 2026. The arc
 hive features the work of the late artist and musician\, T. Scot Halpin. T
 hroughout his life\, Halpin infused his work with positive\, intentional\,
  healing energy\, creating work that is both upbeat and uplifting. The sal
 e includes holiday gifts starting at $10 and original drawings and paintin
 gs for under $100. \n As part of the Open House\, it is also the tradition
  of the Archive to invite local non-profit organizations\, who have fundra
 ising auctions to stop by the print sale and select a piece for their auct
 ion. The Archive is proud of these donations which have gone on to provide
  support for important local community care organizations and local arts p
 rograming.\n This year's Open House & Art Sale will feature the work of ar
 tist David Ebbinghouse. Along with his fine art prints and silk screened t
 -shirts will be featured a collection of hand-made ornaments fashioned fro
 m recycled materials and found objects. Proceeds from the sale of these or
 naments will be donated to Bloomington’s Middleway House.
LOCATION:T. Scot Halpin Archive\, 331 East Glendora Drive\, Bloomington\, 
 Indiana 47408
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/t-scot-halpin-archive-202
 6-open-house-and-holiday-art-sale-09-11-2026-10-41-55
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
