BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gingerbread House Contest
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261206T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261206T150000
UID:291c8aa03db25983b893f5b73c8f5fa8@ipm.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/b8c4
 686/2147483647/strip/true/crop/1028x1028+0+0/resize/254x254!/quality/90/?u
 rl=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F52%2F2d%2F978ff35d487ab1
 bddd2fadfc5118%2F2026ghc-web.png
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Bedford Public Library\nGet ready to unleash your
  creativity and join our Gingerbread House Contest\, a festive fundraiser 
 supporting our local library! Bedford Public Library challenges you to des
 ign and create the most festive\, fun\, or fantastical gingerbread house y
 ou can imagine. This is your chance to shine and compete for the title of 
 Best Gingerbread House in one of four categories: Youth (17 & under)\, Adu
 lts/Family\, Business\, and Nonprofit.\n How It Works:\n - Free to Enter: 
 Sign up to participate and submit your gingerbread creation by November 30
 .\n- Voting: From November 30 - December 14\, all entries will be on displ
 ay for the community to admire. Visitors can cast their votes by purchasin
 g tickets\, with each vote counting toward the best house in each category
 :\n$1 = 1 ticket/vote\n$5 = 6 tickets/votes\n$20 = 25 tickets/votes\n- You
 r Vote Matters: Every ticket purchase helps fund essential library program
 s\, services\, and community outreach\, ensuring that we can continue offe
 ring free resources\, events\, and a welcoming space for all.\n How to Sig
 n Up:\n - Sign Up Online - When signing up online\, simply tell us which c
 ategory you will be competing in (Youth\, Adults/Family\, Business\, or No
 nprofit). If you’re entering as a business or group\, you can sign up un
 der your business name or group name.\n- Sign Up In Person - Drop by the l
 ibrary to sign up in person! Our staff will be happy to assist you with yo
 ur registration\, help you select a category\, and answer any questions yo
 u may have.\n Construction Guidelines:\n- All visible components must be e
 dible. This includes walls\, roof\, decorations\, and landscaping.\n- The 
 base may be non-edible (e.g. cardboard or wood)\, but it must be fully cov
 ered by edible materials.\n- No kits allowed. Entries must be homemade and
  original.\n- Maximum dimensions: size limit 18x18x18.\n- All entries must
  be family-friendly and include a name card.\n Remember\, the deadline for
  all entries is November 30\, so be sure to sign up early and start buildi
 ng your masterpiece! We can’t wait to see what you come up with.\n Mark 
 Your Calendars! Voting will take place between November 30 - December 14\,
  and winners will be announced on our social media.\n Join us for a fun\, 
 festive\, and impactful event this holiday season and help us build a brig
 hter future for the library and our community!\nTickets: https://bedfordpl
 .librarycalendar.com/event/gingerbread-house-contest-2570
