BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Advanced Screening: All Creatures Great and Small Season 7 Premier
 e
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261206T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261206T140000
UID:8863fc890805998d2454d7917d80d0ea@ipm.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/b62a
 59f/2147483647/strip/true/crop/4800x3202+0+0/resize/254x169!/quality/90/?u
 rl=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F78%2Fab%2Fafe91f2340f287
 ce440067fb6e75%2Facgas7-firstlook-5.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Presented by WFIU/WTIU\nIf you need some soothing escapism\, t
 he pets and vets of this beloved dramedy are just the ticket. Join us for 
 a sneak preview of season seven's first episode before its official premie
 re on Masterpiece on PBS in January!\n About All Creatures Great and Small
  Season 7\, Episode 1 Season 7 of All Creatures Great and Small returns vi
 ewers to the beautiful Yorkshire Dales in 1946. With the war finally over
 \, Skeldale House is full once again and livelier than ever as our beloved
  characters reunite under one roof and look ahead to a hopeful new chapter
  where James is excited about recent developments in veterinary medicine\,
  although a new vet in the area threatens the status quo. Packed with warm
 th\, humor\, and community spirit\, this season brings more heartwarming t
 ales of people and animals alike. [50 min\; drama\; English]\nTickets: htt
 ps://cinema.indiana.edu/upcoming-films/screening/2026-fall-sunday-december
 -6-100pm
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East 7th Street\, Bloomington\, Indiana 47405
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/advanced-screening-all-cr
 eatures-great-and-small-season-7-premiere-04-11-2026-12-08-16
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:“The Nutcracker” by Peter Ilyich Tchaikovsky
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261206T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261206T235900
UID:7dd12ca232d97d781fa1074f2e92ed42@ipm.org
DESCRIPTION:NATIONAL OVATION\n Viewers across the country applauded this c
 ontemporary take on the classic ballet featuring the iconic score by Peter
  Ilyich Tchaikovsky when the Emmy-nominated production aired nationally on
  American Public Television last season.\n This bold vision from Jacobs fa
 culty choreographer Sasha Janes shattered stereotypes coast to coast while
  telling the story of inquisitive young Marie and the gift she receives fr
 om her mysterious Aunt Drosselmeier\, who encourages her to unlock the pow
 er of her imagination.\n Join Marie on her incredible adventure as she lea
 rns that magic is everywhere—even in a seemingly ordinary wooden nutcrac
 ker.\n Artistic Staff\nChoreographer\nSasha Janes\n Conductor\nArthur Fage
 n\n Set Designer\nThaddeus Strassberger\n Costume Designer\nLinda Pisano\n
  Video Designer\nGreg Emetaz\n Lighting Designer\nDriscoll Otto\n Wig & Ma
 keup Designer\nKarine Ivey\nTickets: https://am.ticketmaster.com/iumac/buy
LOCATION:Musical Arts Center\, 201 S. Eagleson Ave\, Bloomington\, Indiana
  47405
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/the-nutcracker-by-peter-i
 lyich-tchaikovsky-11-09-2026-15-09-09
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Christmas Season with the Columbus Symphony Orchestra
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261206T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261206T163000
UID:0740f9ddccb4e1cf2ad4ae1812a07fca@ipm.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/a0ce
 31b/2147483647/strip/true/crop/1920x1080+0+0/resize/254x143!/quality/90/?u
 rl=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3a%2Fac%2F492c332848e991
 8f31507d24cfa0%2Fdec-concert.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Columbus Symphony Orchestra\nThe holiday season i
 s approaching!\nMake sure to mark your calendars and come celebrate the ho
 liday season with the Columbus Symphony Orchestra! \n See what we have pla
 nned: \nColeridge-Taylor: Christmas Overture\nAdam: Cantique de Noel\nChri
 stmas Carols sing-along\nKaprálová: Christmas Prelude\nCorelli: Christma
 s Concerto\, Op. 6 No. 8\nHerbert: March of the Toys from Babes in Toyland
 \nAnderson: Sleigh Ride\nFeatured soloist: Jenny Heichelbech\n Come early!
  The Andrews Strings Studio led by Laura Andrews will have a pre-concert p
 erformance starting at 3:00pm. \n ﻿As per tradition\, this is a FREE con
 cert – our gift to the Columbus community! No tickets are required with 
 free admission. Seating is first come\, first served.\n This event is made
  possible in part by the Columbus Area Arts Council\, and the Indiana Arts
  Commission\, which receives support from the State of Indiana and the Nat
 ional Endowment for the Arts.\nBring the family\, tell your coworkers\, or
  just treat yourself! Be prepared for a trip down memory lane and look for
 ward to enjoying home-baked goods after the concert\, courtesy of the Colu
 mbus Symphony Orchestra musicians!\nTickets: https://csoindiana.org/christ
 mas-season-with-the-cso
LOCATION:The Commons\, 300 Washington Street\, Columbus\, Indiana 47201
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/christmas-season-with-the
 -columbus-symphony-orchestra-08-11-2026-14-52-45
