BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Straight No Chaser
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261210T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261210T235900
UID:1dad04a078b759c64a4ff4b8522ec0cc@ipm.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/3351
 ad9/2147483647/strip/true/crop/1080x1080+0+0/resize/254x254!/quality/90/?u
 rl=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F89%2F1f%2F730f4e884e4fb5
 0c221c4d61cd58%2Fsnc-1080x1080.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Presented by IU Auditorium\nThe holiday season is not complete
  without the return of a cappella sensations Straight No Chaser—born rig
 ht here at Indiana University. The group has become synonymous with the so
 und of the holidays\, delivering crowd-pleasing arrangements with humor\, 
 heart\, and flawless harmonies. This year’s performance will be part of 
 their nationwide Making Spirits Bright Tour.\n The nine-man act\, includin
 g Walter Chase\, Jerome Collins\, Seggie Isho\, Michael Luginbill\, Steve 
 Morgan\, Luke Bob Robinson\, Jasper Smith\, Tyler Trepp\, and Freedom Youn
 g\, has served as a festive blend of harmonious voices for three decades.
 \n This year’s tour is a gift that requires no wrapping and one that eve
 ryone delights in sharing. To date\, the band has sold more than three mil
 lion albums worldwide\, sold more than 1.5 million tickets worldwide\, ear
 ned 100 million+ YouTube views\, and racked up more than a billion streams
 .\nTickets: https://www.iuauditorium.com/events/detail/snc-2026
LOCATION:IU Auditorium\, 1211 East 7th Street\, Bloomington\, Indiana 4740
 5
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/straight-no-chaser-05-08-
 2026-12-56-55
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Annie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261211T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261211T213000
UID:109b603a3baf097a9d18eb0e6921ee02@ipm.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/0c3f
 020/2147483647/strip/true/crop/2400x2400+0+0/resize/254x254!/quality/90/?u
 rl=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F21%2F3f%2F296d13f549fbb6
 188dda92a02113%2Fsq-annie-4.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Constellation Stage + Screen\nConstellation Stage
  & Screen presents “Annie” on stage December 10\, 2026 - January 3\, 2
 027 at the Waldron Auditorium.\n Discover the magic of Annie\, the iconic 
 Broadway musical that has captured hearts for generations! The timeless ta
 le of Little Orphan Annie follows a tenacious young girl whose unbreakable
  optimism leads her on an unforgettable journey from a New York City orpha
 nage to a place she can finally call home. Featuring one of Broadway’s m
 ost memorable scores\, including “It’s the Hard-Knock Life\,” “Eas
 y Street\,” “N.Y.C.” and the endlessly-uplifting “Tomorrow\,” An
 nie is a delightful theatrical experience for the entire family. \n See Co
 nstellation’s website for more information\, including a detailed perfor
 mance schedule. Learn more and find tickets at https://seeconstellation.or
 g/kids/annie/\nTickets: https://seeconstellation.org/kids/annie/
LOCATION:Waldron Auditorium\, 122 S Walnut St\, Bloomington\, Indiana 4740
 4
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/annie-24-08-2026-10-39-57
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stone Belt's Pancake Breakfast\, Silent Auction\, & Holiday Art Sa
 le
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261211T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261211T120000
UID:506ed7858b88bd808a1f8a69e99de800@ipm.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/0b8c
 a00/2147483647/strip/true/crop/1080x1080+0+0/resize/254x254!/quality/90/?u
 rl=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2F0c%2Ff041c8ea4dbbb9
 66a1a86b847df6%2F2026-pancake-breakfast-holiday-art-sale-silent-auction-in
 stagram-1.png
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Stone Belt\nStop by Stone Belt on December 11th f
 or a plate full of pancakes\, tons of community cheer\, and the opportunit
 y to purchase (or win!) meaningful holiday gifts!\n Shop the Holiday Art S
 ale for a wide selection of beautiful artwork\, calendars\, note cards\, a
 nd more – all created by talented Stone Belt artists! 100% of artwork sa
 le proceeds go directly to the artist.\n Make yourself a plate at the Panc
 ake Breakfast! Stone Belt clients and volunteers will be flipping pancakes
  all morning\, and will have coffee\, hot cocoa and more available to go a
 longside! Spend time with family and friends\, enjoy breakfast\, and hear 
 holiday hits performed by the All Abilities Choir.\n And this year our Sil
 ent Auction kicks off on Friday\, December 4th\, and closes the day of the
  Pancake Breakfast\, Friday\, December 11th at 6:00 pm! Place your bids on
 line throughout the week\, or bid in person at the breakfast. The auction 
 features an array of exciting goods from local businesses and restaurants
 \, travel deals\, one-of-a-kind experiences\, and more! Don't miss your ch
 ance to win holiday deals!
LOCATION:Stone Belt\, 2815 E 10th St.\, Bloomington\, Indiana 47403
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/stone-belts-pancake-break
 fast-silent-auction-amp-holiday-art-sale-28-10-2026-13-04-10
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
