BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MLK & the Black Press: 200 Years of Pleading Our Own Cause
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20270118T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20270118T193000
UID:ce5a63dd9a63e953a6abdfae45aa1a52@ipm.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/a2c4
 0cc/2147483647/strip/true/crop/300x300+0+0/resize/254x254!/quality/90/?url
 =http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F33%2F1e%2F822a3a94432499a6
 00fc3d005e1a%2Fmlk-2027-facebook-post-300-x-300-px.png
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Birthday Celebration C
 ommission\nThe Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Birthday Celebration Commission 
 presents its annual event honoring the legacy of Dr. Martin Luther King Jr
 . Through remarks from community leaders\, performances by the African Ame
 rican Choral Ensemble\, and a keynote speech from award-winning investigat
 ive journalist Sandra Chapman\, this event will explore the relationship b
 etween the American press and the civil rights movement led by Dr. King an
 d his contemporaries.\nTickets: https://buskirkchumley.org/events/2027-dr-
 martin-luther-king-jr-birthday-celebration-event-january-18-2027/
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington\, Indi
 ana 47408
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/mlk-amp-the-black-press-2
 00-years-of-pleading-our-own-cause-06-11-2026-13-25-46
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
